    "title": "Reichard, Policy Committee Host Hearing on Strengthening Industrial Competitiveness in Pennsylvania",
    "url": "https://repreichard.com/News/37679/Press-Releases/Reichard--Policy-Committee-Host-Hearing-on-Strengthening-Industrial-Competitiveness-in-Pennsylvania",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Reichard, Policy Committee Host Hearing on Strengthening Industrial Competitiveness in Pennsylvania\nMarch 13, 2026\nWHAT:\nHouse Republican Policy Committee Chairman David H. Rowe (R-Snyder/Union/Mifflin/Juniata), Rep. Chad Reichard (R-Franklin) and other lawmakers will host a hearing titled “Built in Pennsylvania: Strengthening Industrial Competitiveness” to examine how policymakers can ensure Pennsylvania’s regulatory environment, energy policies and infrastructure systems support — not hinder — the ability of employers to compete and grow from Pennsylvania.\nWHO:\nTestifiers will include Mike Reed, vice president and general manager – North America operations, Manitowoc Cranes – Shady Grove; Gustavo Casagrandi, general manager, Volvo Construction Equipment, and Mike Ross, president, Franklin County Area Development Corporation.\nWHEN:\nTuesday, March 17, at 11:30 a.m.\nWHERE:\nManitowoc,\n1565 Buchanan Trail E., Shady Grove, PA 17256\nLIVESTREAM:\nBarring any technical difficulties, the hearing will be streamed online at\npolicycommittee.com\n.\nMedia contact:\nNancy Nilson, 717-260-6238,\nnnilson@pahousegop.com\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "Republican members of the Pennsylvania House, including Rep. Chad Reichard and Policy Committee Chairman David Rowe, are holding a public hearing on March 17, 2026 at a manufacturing facility in Shady Grove to discuss how state regulations, energy policy, and infrastructure affect industrial businesses. Business representatives from Manitowoc Cranes, Volvo Construction Equipment, and a local economic development organization are scheduled to testify. This is an informational hearing, not a vote or new legislation.",
