  {
    "title": "Reichard to Host Community-Improvement Tax Credit Workshop",
    "url": "https://repreichard.com/News/37666/Press-Releases/Reichard-to-Host-Community-Improvement-Tax-Credit-Workshop",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Reichard to Host Community-Improvement Tax Credit Workshop\nMarch 9, 2026\nWAYNESBORO – Area business owners are invited to attend a workshop hosted by Rep. Chad Reichard (R-Franklin) on Pennsylvania’s Neighborhood Assistance Program, a tax credit program that benefits the community.\nThe workshop will be held at the Greater Waynesboro Chamber of Commerce, 118 Walnut St., #111, Waynesboro, on Friday, March 20, from 1-3 p.m. Madra Clay, the central regional director with the Department of Economic and Community Development (DCED), will lead the discussion.\nAttendees will learn about the tax credit program that incentivizes businesses to contribute to charitable non-profit organizations by offering a tax credit for their contributions. A tax credit of up to 65% can be awarded.\n“Pennsylvania’s Neighborhood Assistance Program is a great opportunity for businesses to support projects that strengthen our communities while also receiving a meaningful tax credit,” Reichard said. “This workshop will help local business owners better understand how the program works and how they can partner with nonprofits to invest in initiatives that make a real difference in our neighborhoods.”\nA project eligible to receive funds through the program must serve distressed areas or support neighborhood conservation. Projects must fall under one of the following categories: affordable housing programs, community services, crime prevention, education, job training or neighborhood assistance.\nTo register, call Reichard’s office at 717-749-7384, or email jpeters@pahousegop.com.\nRepresentative Chad Reichard\n90th Legislative District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nMedia Contact: Greg Gross\n717.260.6374\nggross@pahousegop.com\nRepReichard.com / Facebook.com/RepReichard\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "Rep. Chad Reichard is hosting a two-hour informational workshop on March 20, 2026, at the Greater Waynesboro Chamber of Commerce. The workshop will be led by a state Department of Economic and Community Development official and will explain Pennsylvania's Neighborhood Assistance Program, which gives businesses tax credits of up to 65% for donating to qualifying nonprofits that serve distressed communities. Business owners can register by calling or emailing Reichard's office.",
      "action_type": "event",
      "topics": [
        "economy",
        "education",
        "housing"
      ],
      "spin_flag": false
    }
  },
  {
    "title": "Reichard: Funding for Fire, EMS Companies Awarded",
    "url": "https://repreichard.com/News/37554/Press-Releases/Reichard--Funding-for-Fire--EMS-Companies-Awarded",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Reichard: Funding for Fire, EMS Companies Awarded\nFebruary 13, 2026\nWAYNESBORO\n– Rep. Chad Reichard (R-Franklin) announced nearly $110,000 in grant funding has been awarded to fire and emergency medical services in the district through the Office of the State Fire Commissioner’s Fire Company and Emergency Medical Service Grant Program.\n“Each day, our brave fire and EMS personnel answer the call, at all hours, to help those in need,” Reichard said. “We owe them thanks and support so they have the training and equipment they need to help us in our times of need.”\n•\nMercersburg Montgomery Peters and Warren (EMS): $8,740.\n•\nMercersburg Montgomery Peters and Warren (Fire): $15,312.\n•\nMont Alto Ambulance Association: $15,000.\n•\nMont Alto Volunteer Fire Co.: $14,899.\n•\nRescue Hose Company No. 1 of Greencastle: $12,014.\n•\nSouth Mountain Volunteer Fire and Ambulance (Fire): $13,663.\n•\nWaynesboro Ambulance Squad Inc.: $15,000.\n•\nWaynesboro Volunteer Fire Department: $26,487.\nAll funding comes from the proceeds from slot machine gaming, not General Fund tax revenue. Projects eligible for funding include construction or renovation of a fire or ambulance company facility, purchase or repair of equipment, training, recruitment and retention, public education about fire prevention, and reduction of existing debt.\nRepresentative Chad Reichard\n90th Legislative District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nMedia Contact: Greg Gross\n717.260.6374\nggross@pahousegop.com\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "Eight fire and EMS organizations in Franklin County's 90th Legislative District received a combined $110,115 in state grants through the Office of the State Fire Commissioner's grant program. The funding, sourced from slot machine gaming revenue, can be used for equipment, training, facility improvements, recruitment, and debt reduction. Rep. Reichard announced the awards but did not author the grant program.",
