    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Reichard Joins in Support of Bill to Modernize Small Games\nOctober 21, 2026\nHARRISBURG – With approval in the Legislature, a bill to modernize Pennsylvania’s small games of chance law is one step away from becoming law. Rep. Chad Reichard (R-Franklin) announced his support of the bill to assist local veterans, social clubs and fire companies.\nHouse Republicans led an effort to amend\nSenate Bill 398\nto increase the weekly prize limit from $35,000 to $60,000 and increase the amount of proceeds clubs can keep for operational expenses.\n“This is a once-in-a-generation change to our small games of chance laws,” Reichard said. “These changes will help ensure local clubs and organizations that give back to our communities will be able to keep their doors open.”\nThe updated legislation would allow clubs to keep 50% of proceeds, up from 40%, for general operating expenses. At least 50% of the remaining proceeds must be earmarked for public interest purposes, such as supporting local sports teams or other community charities.\nThe bill also would allow fire companies with a small games of chance license to hold online raffles in 2027 with debit or credit card payments accepted. Raffle ticket buyers must be at least 18 years of age and in Pennsylvania at the time the tickets are purchased.\n“This legislation provides immediate additional revenue and greater flexibility to clubs and organizations that serve our communities. By allowing these organizations to retain more of the proceeds from small games of chance, we are helping them manage rising operating costs and continue supporting the local causes, charities and community programs that depend on them,” Reichard said. “While this is a major win for clubs, we still need to address the skill games issue. There is certainly still more work to do.”\nSenate Bill 398 is on the governor’s desk for his signature. The price limit and alterations to the distribution of the proceeds would take effect 60 days after it is signed into law.\nRepresentative Chad Reichard\n90th Legislative District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nMedia Contact: Greg Gross\n717.260.6374\nggross@pahousegop.com\nRepReichard.com / Facebook.com/RepReichard\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "The Pennsylvania legislature passed Senate Bill 398, which updates the state's small games of chance law by raising the weekly prize limit from $35,000 to $60,000 and allowing clubs to keep 50% of proceeds (up from 40%) for operating expenses. The bill also permits fire companies to hold online raffles starting in 2027. Rep. Reichard voted in support of the bill, which now awaits the governor's signature.",
